Presented by Para.


A Bish-bashi knockoff suitable for children. In the English language version, the voice over artist talks incredibly quickly. The reason is that, in order to minimise the reprogramming, the new ADPCM samples had to take up the same space as the original Japanese ones. Since Japanese sentences are, in general, shorter (due to the phonetic nature of the alphabet) time was very tight (Even at that speed, she still didn't manage all the samples required).

