$info=docastle,docastl2,docastlo,
$bio

Mr. Do's Castle (c) 09/1983 Universal.


For the second game of the Mr.Do! series, the clown finds himself in a traditional 'platforms 'n' ladders' game. Each level is made up of around six floors, all joined by interconnecting ladders. Some of these are fixed, and some can be pushed left or right from the top of the ladder. In-game enemies are in the form of unicorns. Mr. Do is armed with a hammer, which is used to knock out floor stones. This creates holes in the platforms, forming traps for the unicorns to fall into. Mr.Do! himself can drop through the holes to the platform below, which can be a very handy escape route in the event of him finding himself cornered by the Unicorns.


- TECHNICAL -


