$info=outrun,outrunb,outrun1,outrun2,
$bio

Out Run (c) 11/1986 Sega.


Taking the wheel of a red FERRARI Testarossa, the player races through lush, colourful levels - all packed with 'civilian' traffic - attempting to reach the end-of-level goal before the tight time limit expires. At the end of each stage, the player is presented with a fork in the road : a unique innovation that, for the first time in the history of racing games, gave the player a choice of which route he or she wanted to take through the game.


- TECHNICAL -


Main CPU : (2x) 68000 (@ 10 Mhz)

Sound CPU : Z80 (@ 4 Mhz)

Sound Chips : YM2151 (@ 4 Mhz), Sega (@ 4 Mhz)


Screen orientation : Horizontal

Video resolution : 320 x 224 pixels

Aspect Ratio : 4/3

Screen refresh : 60.00 Hz

Colors palette : 12288


Player : 1

Control : paddle

Button : 1


- TRIVIA -


Out Run's gameplay was both tight and instinctive and, together with the superb stage design - each one lovingly rendered with colourful and incredibly fast sprite-scaled graphics - would completely revolutionise not just racing games, but ALL arcade games in general. Out Run is still regarded as perhaps the finest arcade racer (and certainly the finest sprite-driven racer) of all time. This was especially true of the deluxe cabinet version, which featured a fully hydraulic tilting cabinet (resembling a red Ferrari Testorosa), with a powerful speaker system situated directly behind the player's head. The sublime music still captivates many fans today, although the sublime 'Magical Sound Shower' is generally regarded as the finest of the in-game three tunes ('Magical Sound Shower', 'Passing Breeze' and 'Splash Wave') on offer. The final tune, 'Last Wave', is only played on the high-score board.


Unlike many realistic simulations, like Atari's "Pole Position", Out Run was the original 'boyracer' experience. It symbolised the spirit of the 80s, with a convertible Ferrari Testarossa, blonde bimbo in the passenger seat, thumping music, and numerous crashes. Upon crashing, your car wouldn't just explode, or come to a sudden halt like in many games, it flipped into the air, and rolled over the terrain, throwing the occupants out.


Sega didn't actually have (nor indeed seek) permission from Ferrari to use one of their cars for the game. This inevitably led to a degree of bad feeling and threats of litigation between the two companies. They have since settled their differences, however, as Sega acquired an official licencse to use the Ferrari range in its 2003 sequel, "Out Run 2".


Opponent cars list:

* 1972 Volkswagen Beetle

* 1971 Chevrolet Corvette

* 1985 Porsche Carrera 911 Turbo

* 1985 BMW 325i Cabriolet E30

* Lorry


An Out Run machine is played by Jake Gyllenhaal in the movie 'Donnie Darko'.


Alfa Records released a limited-edition soundtrack album for this game (Sega Taikan Game Special - 28XA-198) on 12/1987.

Scitron released a soundtrack album for this game (Outrun/SEGA S.S.T. - PCCB-00081) on 02/1992. Composition by SEGA Sound Team and arrangement by SEGA S.S.T. Band. The first 3 tracks are arranged versions.


- UPDATES -


In the Deluxe version, all the courses are in a different order.


- TIPS AND TRICKS -


* Super Speed : Instead of just pressing the accelerator all the way when you're about to start, you should instead try to keep the gas in 'the high greens' and just below red. The exact moment the green light goes on you should give it as much gas as possible thereby starting up much faster. Instead of shifting at app. 170mph you should change gears at about 120 mph to avoid slowdown. This hint earns you app. 1 second. This trick works every time you have to start from 0 mph but is difficult to time right when you don't have the green light for timing.


* Secret Credit Message : Right before the road forks, press and hold Start. When you choose one of the roads and the other one disappears from view, a secret credit message will come up on the screen.


* Fatest Route : The fastest route for finishing the game is Right (Devil's Canyon), Left (Snowy Alps), Right (Wheatfield), Right (Autobahn).


- SERIES -


1. Out Run (1986)

2. Out Run 3-D (1989, Sega Master System)

3. Battle Out Run (1989, Sega Master System)

4. Turbo Out Run (1989)

5. Out Run Europa (1991, Sega Game Gear)

6. Out Runners (1992)

7. Out Run 2019 (1993, Sega Mega Drive)

8. Out Run 2 (2003)


- STAFF -


Designed by : Yu Suzuki (YU.)

Music by : Hiroshi Miyauchi (MIY)

From highscore table : (BIN), (KAG), (MAT), (IKA), (A.O)


- PORTS -


