$info=rotd,
$bio

Rage of the Dragons (c) 06/2002 Evoga / Playmore.


Rage of the Dragons is an original fighting game with 14 selectable fighters plus Abubo (sub-boss, hidden character) and Johann (final boss).


- TECHNICAL -


SNK Neo-Geo MVS hardware

Game ID : 0264


Main CPU : 68000 (@ 12 Mhz)

Sound CPU : Z80 (@ 4 Mhz)

Sound Chips : YM2610 (@ 8 Mhz)


Screen orientation : Horizontal

Video resolution : 304 x 224 pixels

Aspect Ratio : 4/3

Screen refresh : 59.19 Hz

Colors palette : 4096


Players : 2

Control : 8-way Joystick

Buttons : 4


- TRIVIA -


Rage of the Dragons was the first fighting game by Evoga (This game was developed on agreement between MEXICO (EVOGA) & JAPAN (BREZZA SOFT & NOISE FACTORY).


Evoga tried to make a new "Double Dragon" game. Evoga tried to buy the Double Dragon copyright from Technos Japan but they refused to sell it. They decided to do an homage game. The game is not directly related to the original Technos' Double Dragon Series, it is inspired on it. In Rage of the Dragons the names are William 'Billy' Lewis, James 'Jimmy' Lewis and 'Abubo' (instead of Abobo, Jimmy Lee and Billy Lee). One funny thing about these Evoga characters is that they appear in Noise Factory's Matrimeele, based in the Power Instinct series by Atlus.


- TIPS AND TRICKS -


* Play As Abubo : At the character select screen, press quickly Up(x4), Down(x3), Left(x2), Right. Abobo should appear on center.


