$info=sichuan2,sichuana,
$bio

Sichuan II (c) 1989 Tamtex.


Szechuan-style solitaire mahjong.


- TECHNICAL -


Main CPU : Z80 (@ 6 Mhz)

Sound CPU : Z80 (@ 3.579645 Mhz)

Sound Chips : YM2151 (@ 3.579545 Mhz), DAC (@ 3.579545 Mhz)


Screen orientation : Horizontal

Video resolution : 512 x 256 pixels

Aspect Ratio : 4/3

Screen refresh : 55.00 Hz

Colors palette : 256


Players : 2

Control : 8-way joystick

Buttons : 3


- TRIVIA -


This game is also known as "Shisensho - Joshiryo-Hen".


'Sichuan' is the Chinese translation of 'Szechuan', which is the largest province in China. The game at hand here is indeed Szechuan-style solitaire mahjong, where the object is to match two identical unblocked tiles until the board is clear. This type of solitaire mahjong is also referred to as "Shisen-Sho". The tile layout presented herein is one of many traditional Chinese Szechuan-style solitaire arrangements.

$end

