- TRIVIA -


Star Fire was the first environmental game, featuring a viewer window. This is the first arcade coin-operated video game to maintain a high score table by accepting and displaying the names of winning players.


A mockup of Star Fire as an upright machine appears in the 1980 movie 'Midnight Madness', but the game was only released as a cockpit. Exidy wanted to get their game into the movie as a marketing tool, but the screen in the cockpit version was too hard to film. So an upright mockup was fabricated.


- TIPS AND TRICKS -


* Secret messages :

1) If you enter 'DBR' it will put 'HI DAVE' on the screen; It's David Rolfe.

2) If you enter 'TZM' it will put 'HI TED' on the screen; It's Ted Michon.

3) If you enter 'SKO' it will put 'HI SUSAN' on the screen for a second or two before showing the high-score table; It's Susan K. Owen, the graphics artists girlfriend (and she also worked for this game as a graphics artist).


- STAFF -


Programmed by : David Rolfe

Graphics by : Ted Michon, Susan Owen


- PORTS -


