$info=yiear,yiear2,
$bio

Yie Ar Kung-Fu (c) 01/1985 Konami.


Oolong the Kung-Fu fighter fights different martial artists for the respect of his dojo!


- TECHNICAL -


Game ID : GX407


Main CPU : M6809 (@ 1.152 Mhz)

Sound Chips : SN76496 (@ 1.536 Mhz), VLM5030 (@ 3.58 Mhz)


Screen orientation : Horizontal

Video resolution : 256 x 224 pixels

Aspect Ratio : 4/3

Screen refresh : 60.00 Hz

Colors palette : 32


Players : 2

Control : 8-way joystick

Buttons : 2


- TRIVIA -


A true classic, Yie Ar Kung-Fu, while somewhat limited in gameplay terms, was very innovative in its own right. It was the first one-on-one fighter to offer a progression of truly different opponents for the player to defeat in order to progress through the game. This is something that would later be adopted by Capcom for its legendary "Street Fighter" series, as well as SNK and countless others.


- SERIES -


1. Yie Ar Kung-Fu (1985)

