$info=zzyzzyxx,zzyzzyx2,
$bio

Zzyzzyxx (c) 11/1982 Advanced Microcomputer / Cinematronics.


Help Boris get to Lola. Life would be fun if women were that easy, but as in real life it's not that easy. To please her you need to collect some gifts for her. Only when she is pleased with what you collected can you dare to come near, just to start over on the next screen.


- TECHNICAL -


Main CPU : Z80 (@ 3 Mhz)

Sound CPU : Z80 (@ 1.5 Mhz)

Sound Chips : AY-3-8910 (@ 1.5 Mhz)


Screen orientation : Vertical

Video resolution : 224 x 256 pixels

Aspect Ratio : 3/4

Screen refresh : 60.00 Hz

Colors palette : 32


Players : 2

Control : Joystick 2-way

Button : 1


- TRIVIA -


A prototype of this game is known as "Brix", which was renamed to Zzyzzyxx before release.


Note : This game is always the last to appear alphabetically in a complete arcade games database. :)


Cinematronics never designed a dedicated cabinet for this game. It can be found in any of the generic black cabinets of the day (they used several different ones during the production run). No sideart was made, just a control panel overlay, marquee, and two stickers (which were applied to a generic glass monitor bezel). A far cry from the standard floor to ceiling art that decorated most games in the early eighties. This game uses a unique wiring harness that is not compatible with any other titles, although it could be rigged up in any vertical cabinet with a little work.

$end
